# The table timer, pauses and async deadlines (TEMPO-03/04/05). The clock runs only while the game
# is live: everyone still in it at the table, and no pause. A player who is away has a deadline for
# each decision: a reminder halfway, then the game is flagged for a judge. Nothing is ever done on
# their behalf.
seed 12
timelimit 2h
deadline 24h
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *8
library A "Iron Ward" *20
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *8
library B "Signal Fire" *20
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *8
library C "Quick Feed" *20
start
expect elapsed 0m
expect timeup no

# Everyone at the table: the clock runs.
present A yes
present B yes
present C yes
expect tempo live
wait 30m
expect elapsed 30m

# Bob needs a break. While paused nothing happens and the clock waits; the pause ends by itself.
B> pause 3
log public B paused the game for 3 minutes
expect paused yes
reject:not-now A> next
reject:forbidden C> resume
reject:not-now A> pause 2
wait 1m
expect paused yes
expect elapsed 30m
wait 2m
expect paused no
log public The pause is over
expect elapsed 30m
# Pauses are short, and whoever asked can lift one early.
reject:invalid B> pause 6
B> pause 5
B> resume
log public B resumed the game

# Someone leaves: async, so the clock waits for them.
present C no
expect tempo async
wait 2h
expect elapsed 30m
expect timeup no
present C yes

# The time limit is reached after 90 more minutes of live play.
wait 90m
expect timeup yes
log public Time is up: the game ends with the current action, or at the end of this phase

# Alice, whose turn it is, leaves. Her decision gets a deadline: a reminder at 12 h, and at 24 h a
# judge is asked to step in. Her turn isn't played for her.
present A no
expect deadline A pending
expect deadline B none
wait 12h
expect deadline A reminded
wait 12h
expect deadline A expired
log public A ran out of time for a decision (their turn); a judge will step in
expect waiting A:phase
# Back at the table, the deadline goes away.
present A yes
expect deadline A none
